cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CrystalPilot, please cite it as below."
title: "CrystalPilot: a browser interface for XDS crystallographic data processing"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Elias
    given-names: Mikael
version: 0.6.8
date-released: 2026-09-20
license: GPL-3.0-only
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22756729
repository-code: "https://github.com/mikaelhelias/CrystalPilot"
abstract: >-
  CrystalPilot is a user-friendly, consolidated interface for X-ray diffraction
  data processing with XDS: project management, XDS.INP and XSCALE.INP editing,
  automatic analysis of IDXREF, CORRECT and XSCALE results with resolution
  cut-off criteria, AutoPilot processing of single data sets or batches,
  automatic Table 1, a frame viewer, and work modes for learning.
keywords:
  - crystallography
  - X-ray diffraction
  - XDS
  - data processing
  - structural biology
